@@ -1,5 +1,32 @@
 # The location-analysis agent graph

+## Static botanical species profiles
+
+`botanical_species_profiles.species_information` is registered in `WAREHOUSE_TOOLS` under the alias
+`species_profile_information` (its module-level name collides with the existing companion/authoring
+tool of the same name in `tools.py`). It is exposed identically through the Anthropic graph, OpenAI
+`tool_schemas()` and MCP `tools/list`/`tools/call`. It accepts the complete canonical
+authority/version/taxon identity and an exact `bspf-<sha256>` profile release. It never resolves a
+name, reads a latest pointer, queries editable `agri.species`/`companion_relationships` rows, or
+performs a species ranking.
+
+The plane reads the immutable manifest and Parquet artifacts through the same process-wide bounded
+worker admission as environmental reads. Storage is configured lazily with
+`BotoAvailabilityStorage.from_settings`; `use_profile_storage` injects a local store for tests. The
+response includes all six distinct evidence sections, raw and normalized assertions, source versions
+and licences, decision identifiers and the content-bound release manifest. Assertion pages follow a
+bound cursor; `evidence_complete` on a field tells the caller whether the current page already
+carries every assertion it cites.
+
+Excluded from `WAREHOUSE_TOOLS_FOR_WEB` and from the sufficiency-budget denominator alongside
+`species_information`, for the same reason: a static reference lookup is not selected-day
+environmental coverage and should neither gate the web-search fallback nor count against how much
+search budget a thin environmental result buys.
+
 ## Warehouse tools
 See `tools.py` for the full published surface.
